  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "2 Kings",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 22,
    "summary": "Josiah reigns in righteousness in Judah—Hilkiah repairs the temple and finds the book of the law—Josiah sorrows because of the wickedness of his fathers—Huldah prophesies wrath upon the people but blessings upon Josiah.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Josiah was eight years old when he began to reign, and he reigned thirty and one years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Jedidah, the daughter of Adaiah of Boscath.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 6,
            "text": "2 Chr. 34:1 (1–33)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 10
          },
          {
            "start": 123,
            "end": 126
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 22:1",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And he did that which was right in the sight of the Lord, and walked in all the way of David his father, and turned not aside to the right hand or to the left.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 25
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 22:2",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass in the eighteenth year of king Josiah, that the king sent Shaphan the son of Azaliah, the son of Meshullam, the scribe, to the house of the Lord, saying,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 63
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 22:3",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Go up to Hilkiah the high priest, that he may sum the silver which is brought into the house of the Lord, which the keepers of the door have gathered of the people:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "1 Chr. 6:13; Ezra 7:1."
          },
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 60,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 12:4."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
