          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 22:13",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "So Hilkiah the priest, and Ahikam, and Achbor, and Shaphan, and Asahiah, went unto Huldah the prophetess, the wife of Shallum the son of Tikvah, the son of Harhas, keeper of the wardrobe; (now she dwelt in Jerusalem in the college;) and they communed with her.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 223,
            "end": 230,
            "text": "IE one of two geographical sections of Jerusalem."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 22:14",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "And she said unto them, Thus saith the Lord God of Israel, Tell the man that sent you to me,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 22:15",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "Thus saith the Lord, Behold, I will bring evil upon this place, and upon the inhabitants thereof, even all the words of the book which the king of Judah hath read:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 124,
            "end": 128,
            "text": "2 Chr. 34:24 (14–27)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 98,
            "end": 102
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 22:16",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "Because they have forsaken me, and have burned incense unto other gods, that they might provoke me to anger with all the works of their hands; therefore my wrath shall be kindled against this place, and shall not be quenched.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 88,
            "end": 95,
            "text": "Jer. 44:8."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Jer. 44:8.",
            "prettyString": "Jeremiah 44:8",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "jeremiah",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 44,
                    "end": 44,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 8,
                        "end": 8
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 22:17",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "But to the king of Judah which sent you to inquire of the Lord, thus shall ye say to him, Thus saith the Lord God of Israel, As touching the words which thou hast heard;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 125,
            "end": 136
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 22:18",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "Because thine heart was tender, and thou hast humbled thyself before the Lord, when thou heardest what I spake against this place, and against the inhabitants thereof, that they should become a desolation and a curse, and hast rent thy clothes, and wept before me; I also have heard thee, saith the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 53,
            "text": "Alma 32:14 (14–15)."
          },
          {
            "start": 194,
            "end": 204,
            "text": "Lev. 26:33 (31–35)."
          },
          {
            "start": 211,
            "end": 216,
            "text": "TG Curse."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 283,
            "end": 288
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Curse.",
            "prettyString": "TG Curse",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
